# Role
You are writing the growth dashboard's data endpoint for TinyWins — the
backend half of "at the end of the period, show how much the user has
grown." It is scoped to **one goal at a time**, because the UI has a goal
picker and renders one goal's history at a time.

# Requirements
Build `src/app/api/growth/route.ts`.

**`GET /api/growth?goalId=<id>`** -> `GrowthResponse`.

- `goalId` is required -> 400 when missing. 404 when the goal doesn't belong
  to the demo user (scope the query by `userId`, don't just look up by id).
- Report over the goal's run: `startDate` through **today, or `endDate` if
  the run already finished** — never past the end of the goal. A goal whose
  `startDate` is in the future reports empty series rather than erroring.
- `pointsSeries`: one entry per day in range, `{ date, earned, penalty }`,
  built with `bucketLedgerByDay` over **goal-scoped** ledger rows only
  (redemptions are account-wide and must not appear in a goal's chart).
  `date` is a short display label from `formatDayLabel`.
- `history`: one entry per day in range, status from `dayStatus`:
  - `"done"` -> include `verdict` from that day's `CheckIn` and `points`
    (the day's earned total).
  - `"skipped"` -> `points: -goal.penaltyPoints`, the **nominal** cost of
    skipping a period. Disclose that the real deduction is written lazily on
    the user's next visit, so its ledger date can differ from the day
    skipped; `summary.netPoints` uses real ledger sums, so headline numbers
    stay exact.
  - `"due"` / `"future"` -> no `points`, no `verdict`.
- `summary`:
  - `checkInsDone` — count of `CheckIn` rows for the goal.
  - `checkInsExpected` — number of days in the reported range.
  - `skips` — count of `"skipped"` history entries (derived from real
    check-in dates, not from penalty rows).
  - `netPoints` — sum of all goal-scoped ledger amounts (earned minus
    penalties), so it can legitimately be negative.

# Interface
Reference `GrowthResponse` and `GoalSummary` from `src/lib/contract.ts`.

# Dependencies
<include>src/lib/growth.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/goals.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/contract.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/prisma.ts</include>

# Acceptance criteria
- Missing `goalId` -> 400; a goal id belonging to another user -> 404.
- A goal created today returns exactly one day in `pointsSeries` and
  `history`, with that day `"due"` (or `"done"` after a check-in) — never
  `"skipped"`.
- A finished goal's range stops at its `endDate`, not today.
- `netPoints` goes negative when penalties exceed earnings.
- Redemption ledger rows never appear in any goal's `pointsSeries`.
